this is the last time Leah Croucher was  seen walking to work in February 2019  more than three and a half years later  her parents say their darkest fears have  come true after the missing person  inquiry became a murder investigation  and now another significant update we  have nominated a suspect in this case  his name is Neil Maxwell  however  Maxwell was found dead on the 20th of  April  2019 having taken his own life  Maxwell was a convicted sexual offender  in the six months before his death  police try to arrest him 18 times for an  alleged sexual assault he's now been  linked to the address in Milton Keynes  where police found human remains  alongside Leah's rucksack and personal  possessions it is unusual to name a  suspect  but we have also learned this week that  during the time when Leah went missing  and whilst the owner of the property was  not in the UK  Maxwell was the only person to have keys  to that property  this property is only around half a mile  away from where Leah Croucher was last  seen and during the police's  door-to-door inquiries they say they  visited it twice before leaving a  leaflet because no one had been  occupying it the only reason Maxwell had  access was because he'd been hired by  the homeowners to carry out some  maintenance work  as forensic examinations continue so  will the lines of inquiry into Maxwell  as police pieced together what exactly  happened to Leah to give her family  answers they've long been waiting for  Aisha zahid Sky News
 

